  "summary": "Malicious code in cs-core-api-phoenix (npm)",
  "details": "cs-core-api-phoenix 5.1.0 is a dependency-confusion package: its postinstall script reads the OS user name and hostname and POSTs them to https://nathanaccacio.com/collect on every install. It targets an internal-looking name and collects data from whoever installs it, without consent.\n\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (0956e91425fb7305b2d25ad7cd93666ecfe8c6c99fd942138a1bef547b4f7716)\nOn `npm install`, the package's postinstall hook executes `node index.js`, which reads `os.userInfo().username` and `os.hostname()` and POSTs them (together with a package identifier) to the hardcoded third-party endpoint `https://nathanaccacio.com/collect` via `https.request`. The package name resembles a core API client, but no advertised functionality explains collecting installer identity at install time, and the destination is not caller-configurable. The behavior fires automatically on default install, discloses the installer's user and host identity to a non-first-party domain, and provides reconnaissance value to the operator of that endpoint.\n",
